    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class and both tests pass. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe locality derivation now prefers the postcode over the city.\n\n**`Region.java`** \u2014 Added a static `forPostcode(String)` method that parses the postcode and finds the region whose inclusive range contains it (reusing the existing `acceptsPostcode`), returning empty when the postcode is null, non-numeric, or in no known range.\n\n**`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Updated `locality(Owner)` to look up the region by postcode first, falling back to the city-to-region table only when the postcode doesn't resolve, then to `\"UNKNOWN\"`:\n\n```java\nreturn Region.forPostcode(owner.getPostcode())\n    .or(() -> Region.forCity(owner.getCity()))\n    .map(Region::name)\n    .orElse(\"UNKNOWN\");\n```\n\nThis returns the same region for known cities (Sydney's 2000 \u2192 NSW) while disambiguating shared city names \u2014 a VIC-range postcode (3000) on an unknown city now yields VIC. Test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 2/2 tests passing, including `coreRegionFromPostcodeRange` and `functionalityPostcodePreferredOverCity`).",
