    "probe_text": "Here is every validation and side-effect applied when creating an owner via `POST /api/owners`, in the exact order it happens. The route is served by `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` (implementing the OpenAPI-generated `OwnersApi`).\n\n## Before the controller body runs\n\n1. **Authorization check** \u2014 `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")` requires the caller to hold `ROLE_OWNER_ADMIN` (enforced only when `petclinic.security.enable=true`). Failure \u2192 `403`.\n2. **Bean Validation of the request body** \u2014 `@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto` is validated by JSR-380 before the method executes. Per-field constraints:\n   - `firstName`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern` (letters, up to 3 space/`'`/`-`-separated words)\n   - `lastName`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern` (as above, optional trailing `.`)\n   - `address`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..255)`\n   - `city`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..80)`\n   - `postcode`: optional, `@Pattern(\"^[0-9]{4}$\")`\n   - `telephone`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`\n   - `email`: optional, `@Size(1..255)`, `@Email`\n   - `registrationDate`: optional `LocalDate`\n   - `sharesHousehold`: no constraint (write-only flag)\n   \n   Failure \u2192 `400` via `handleMethodArgumentNotValidException`.\n\n## Inside `addOwner`, in order\n\n3. **Address normalization (side-effect: mutates DTO)** \u2014 `addressNormalizer.normalize`: trims/collapses whitespace, upper-cases, expands `ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`.\n4. **Blank-field rejection (validation)** \u2014 `rejectBlankOwnerFields`: catches whitespace-only values that `@Size(min=1)` misses \u2192 `InvalidOwnerFieldsException` / `400`.\n5. **Read `sharesHousehold` flag** into a local boolean.\n6. **Postcode validation** \u2014 `rejectInvalidPostcode`: checks the postcode is valid for the city per the `Region` city\u2192postcode-range table \u2192 `InvalidOwnerPostcodeException` / `400`.\n7. **City-capacity check (validation)** \u2014 `rejectCityAtCapacity`: reads all owners; rejects if the city already has 50 owners (`MAX_OWNERS_PER_CITY`) \u2192 `OwnerCityAtCapacityException` / `409`.\n8. **Registration-date defaulting + business-day adjustment (side-effect)** \u2014 `effectiveRegistrationDate` defaults a missing date to today; `businessDay` rolls weekends forward to Monday.\n9. **Daily-limit check (validation)** \u2014 `rejectDailyRegistrationLimit`: rejects if 100 owners (`MAX_OWNERS_PER_DAY`) are already registered on that resolved date \u2192 `DailyOwnerRegistrationLimitException` / `429`.\n10. **Telephone normalization (side-effect + validation)** \u2014 `telephoneNormalizer.normalize` canonicalizes to E.164 and writes it back to the DTO; throws `InvalidOwnerFieldsException` / `400` if it can't (bad prefix, digit count outside 8\u201315, wrong national length).\n11. **Email normalization (side-effect: mutates DTO)** \u2014 `emailNormalizer.normalize` lower-cases the email.\n12. **Map DTO \u2192 `Owner` entity** \u2014 MapStruct `ownerMapper.toOwner`; copies the basic fields only (ignores `id`, `pets`, and the derived fields).\n13. **Set `registrationDate`** on the entity (the business-day-adjusted value).\n14. **Compute & set `customerCode` (side-effect)** \u2014 `nextCustomerCode`: format `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>`, sequence = current owner count in that city + 1 (reads all owners).\n15. **Compute & set `namesakeCount` (side-effect)** \u2014 `namesakeCount`: case-insensitive count of existing owners with the same first+last name (reads all owners).\n16. **Conditionally compute & set `householdId` (side-effect)** \u2014 only if `sharesHousehold` is true: SHA-256 of canonicalized lastName+address, first 16 hex chars.\n17. **Duplicate-identity check (validation)** \u2014 `rejectDuplicateIdentity`: reads all owners; rejects if the identity key (`canonicalTelephone|email|householdId`) already exists \u2192 `DuplicateOwnerIdentityException` / `409`.\n18. **Persist to database (side-effect)** \u2014 `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)` (`@Transactional`) \u2192 `ownerRepository.save` \u2192 `EntityManager.persist` INSERT; `id` is DB-generated (`GenerationType.IDENTITY`).\n19. **Audit log (side-effect)** \u2014 `AUDIT.info(...)` logs id, customerCode, registrationDate, and derived membershipLevel.\n20. **Build response DTO with derived fields** \u2014 `toOwnerDtoWithDerivedFields` populates read-only `bulkSignupWarning` and `identityKey` (plus mapper-derived membershipNumber/level, locality, contactPreference).\n21. **Set `Location` header (side-effect)** \u2014 to `/api/owners/{id}`.\n22. **Return `201 CREATED`** with the owner DTO.\n\n## Notable absences on this path\nThere are **no** JPA lifecycle callbacks (`@PrePersist`/`@PreUpdate`), no entity listeners, no `@CreationTimestamp`/auto-timestamps, no application events, and no email sending \u2014 every derived field and timestamp is set manually in the controller. The `Owner` entity's own Bean Validation constraints (`@NotEmpty`, `@Pattern`, `@Email`, etc.) are **not** re-enforced on this manual save path \u2014 only the DTO constraints in step 2 are enforced. `BCryptPasswordEncoder` exists but is used only for login auth, not owner creation (owners have no password)."
